                                        "entry_id": "0d1695d2-32d6-3192-a647-d8636871664b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A plant with simple stems, like bamboo or sugar cane, or the stem thereof",
                                            "Maize or, rarely, sorghum, when such plants are processed to make molasses (treacle) or sugar"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Southern",
                                            "US",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "689b40ac-a3e7-38e1-aa5d-fb3d7b523999",
                                        "entry_id": "0d1695d2-32d6-3192-a647-d8636871664b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The stem of such a plant adapted for use as a tool",
                                            "A short rod or stick, traditionally of wood or bamboo, used for corporal punishment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fba9213-92ae-4bd1-b694-d12ca14541e9",
                                                "sense_id": "689b40ac-a3e7-38e1-aa5d-fb3d7b523999",
                                                "text": "He stalked behind her simple narrative, a kill-joy parent, hasty, intolerant, keeping a special cane to enforce the authority of his sadistic God[.]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71970351-403f-3af9-bc49-46ce2e75d797",
                                        "entry_id": "0d1695d2-32d6-3192-a647-d8636871664b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The stem of such a plant adapted for use as a tool",
                                            "Corporal punishment by beating with a cane."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "with-definite-article"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e31da26b-0c1e-4fb5-85f9-6a01389f09b2",
                                                "sense_id": "71970351-403f-3af9-bc49-46ce2e75d797",
                                                "text": "The teacher gave his student the cane for throwing paper."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5a109be1-7309-3e1d-b820-d7b5617c9bc8",
                                        "entry_id": "0d1695d2-32d6-3192-a647-d8636871664b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The stem of such a plant adapted for use as a tool",
                                            "A lance or dart made of cane"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b441d02-4f02-43fc-a50a-2fb4c76901c0",
                                                "sense_id": "5a109be1-7309-3e1d-b820-d7b5617c9bc8",
                                                "text": "Judgelike thou sitt'st, to praise or to arraign / The flying skirmish of the darted cane."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e10da0a-0e72-3c90-8ee9-802a5f580f31",
                                        "entry_id": "0d1695d2-32d6-3192-a647-d8636871664b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rod-shaped tool or device, resembling the stem of the plant.",
                                            "A strong short staff used for support or decoration during walking; a walking stick"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c95cb74-acb5-412d-aca9-e61e52c3fb3d",
                                                "sense_id": "9e10da0a-0e72-3c90-8ee9-802a5f580f31",
                                                "text": "After breaking his leg, he needed a cane to walk."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a255c4c4-c566-4b01-97cd-9a40e2a07b21",
                                                "sense_id": "9e10da0a-0e72-3c90-8ee9-802a5f580f31",
                                                "text": "The cane was undoubtedly of foreign make, for it had a solid silver ferrule at one end, which was not English hall–marked."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "970186ac-9915-4bd2-861b-775d5b6474ff",
                                                "sense_id": "9e10da0a-0e72-3c90-8ee9-802a5f580f31",
                                                "text": "Men that I knew around Wapatomac didn't wear high, shiny plug hats, nor yeller spring overcoats, nor carry canes with ivory heads as big as a catboat's anchor, as you might say."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71049ed6-a0cb-3a09-954a-0588983083bb",
                                        "entry_id": "0d1695d2-32d6-3192-a647-d8636871664b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rod-shaped tool or device, resembling the stem of the plant.",
                                            "A length of colored and/or patterned glass rod, used in the specific glassblowing technique called caneworking"
                                        ],
